From a77e608fea260028047d020a0b7ba17bf412332a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ascend-torchtitan <jimmy.eyjc@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 23:45:15 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] npu: implement aten::_flash_attention_forward/_backward on
 npu_fusion_attention

torch.nn.attention.varlen.varlen_attn (and the SDPA flash path) lower to
aten::_flash_attention_forward / _backward, which have no PrivateUse1 kernel:
'NotImplementedError: Could not run aten::_flash_attention_forward ...'.
Callers written against the public flash-attention contract -- e.g.
torchtitan's VarlenAttention -- therefore cannot run on Ascend.

Register PrivateUse1 implementations backed by npu_fusion_attention /
npu_fusion_attention_grad: dense (B,S,N,D) and packed varlen (T,N,D) layouts,
right-aligned causal (sparse_mode 3), left window (sparse_mode 4), GQA. The
kernel's per-sequence head-major softmax statistics are folded into the aten
logsumexp layout ((B,N,S) / (N,T)) and expanded back for the backward with
softmax_sum == 1, which satisfies the kernel's P = exp(S - max) / sum.
Dropout, alibi, paged KV and seqused_k are rejected explicitly.

Validated on Ascend 910B2 / CANN 9.1.0 (torch 2.13.0 + torch_npu 2.13.0rc1):
varlen_attn forward and grads match a fp32 SDPA reference per document
(bf16 tolerance), and torchtitan qwen3 debugmodel with the stock
VarlenAttention (no override) trains 10 steps.
